# Agent/session tooling state. Untracked is not enough - these files sit in the
# working directory, so a `cp -r` or a folder-based publish carries them along.
# One of them is a session replay log.
.omc/
# WARNING: .claude/* not .claude/ - and the negation below only works that way.
# Git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so "!.claude/skills/" placed
# after a bare ".claude/" is silently dead. Excluding the CONTENTS leaves the
# directory walkable so the re-include can take effect.
#
# This matters because .claude/skills/ is read by Claude Code AND by Copilot, so
# it is a file the README tells people to COMMIT. Ignoring it wholesale meant
# this project's own repo excluded the one artefact it ships.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated views. They are derived from the source of truth and regenerating is
# cheap; committing them invites the stale-copy-gets-believed failure this tool
# exists to prevent.
MAP.md
TRAPS.md
CANDIDATES.md
